2,&quot;OwnerID&quot;:132,&quot;DocumentLink&quot;:&quot;\/assets\/Uploads\/Tatauranga-umanga-Maori-Statistics-on-Maori-businesses\/Tatauranga-umanga-Maori-Statistics-on-Maori-businesses-2024\/Download-data\/tatauranga-umanga-maori-statistics-on-maori-businesses-2024-te-reo-maori.xlsx&quot;,&quot;DocumentCategory&quot;:&quot;document&quot;,&quot;DocumentExtension&quot;:&quot;xlsx&quot;,&quot;DocumentFileType&quot;:&quot;Excel spreadsheet&quot;,&quot;DocumentIcon&quot;:&quot;\/_resources\/vendor\/silverstripe\/framework\/client\/images\/app_icons\/document_92.png?m=1786327239&quot;,&quot;DocumentSize&quot;:&quot;96 KB&quot;,&quot;DocumentPreviewImage&quot;:false}],&quot;Heading&quot;:null,&quot;Action&quot;:{&quot;ActionText&quot;:null,&quot;ActionHref&quot;:{&quot;Url&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;Target&quot;:&quot;_self&quot;}},&quot;Presentation&quot;:null},{&quot;ID&quot;:&quot;12351&quot;,&quot;Title&quot;:&quot;CSV files for download - What are CSV files?&quot;,&quot;ClassName&quot;:&quot;TextBlock&quot;,&quot;ShowBlockTitle&quot;:false,&quot;DefaultView&quot;:&quot;Grid&quot;,&quot;Content&quot;:&quot;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=\&quot;what-are-csvs\&quot;&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;What are CSV files?&lt;\/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;CSV files are text files with information separated by commas,&amp;nbsp;saved with the extension .csv.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=\&quot;font-size: 1rem;\&quot;&gt;They allow large amounts of detailed data to be transferred \u2018machine-to-machine\u2019, with little or no reformatting by the user.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can open a CSV file with any spreadsheet, statistics, or analysis program, such as Microsoft Excel, the R statistical environment, or Python.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;CSV files may open in Excel&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=\&quot;font-size: 1rem;\&quot;&gt;by default&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\&quot;font-size: 1rem;\&quot;&gt;, but they are not designed as Excel files. If CSV files are opened in Excel, certain information (eg codes with leading zeros) could be missing. Ideally, they should be imported into a database designed to preserve the CSV format.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;&quot;},{&quot;ID&quot;:&quot;12434&quot;,&quot;Title&quot;:&quot;CSV files for download - Find variable names in Infoshare&quot;,&quot;ClassName&quot;:&quot;TextBlock&quot;,&quot;ShowBlockTitle&quot;:false,&quot;DefaultView&quot;:&quot;Grid&quot;,&quot;Content&quot;:&quot;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=\&quot;infoshare-variables\&quot;&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;Find variable names in Infoshare&lt;\/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Because a CSV file may contain multiple tables from Infoshare, some variable headings have generic labels.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;captionImage leftAlone\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 423px;\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;captionImage leftAlone\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 402px;\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;captionImage leftAlone\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 402px;\&quot;&gt;&lt;img width=\&quot;402\&quot; height=\&quot;73\&quot; alt=\&quot;An example of a CSV file (opened in Excel) with generic variable names.\&quot; src=\&quot;\/assets\/Uploads\/Tools\/CSV-files-for-download\/Infoshare-variable-names.png\&quot; loading=\&quot;lazy\&quot; class=\&quot;leftAlone ss-htmleditorfield-file image\&quot;&gt;\n\n\n&lt;p class=\&quot;caption leftAlone\&quot;&gt;An example of a CSV file (opened in Excel) with generic variable names.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You can find the names of these variables in Infoshare.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;captionImage leftAlone\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 600px;\&quot;&gt;&lt;img width=\&quot;600\&quot; height=\&quot;412\&quot; alt=\&quot;Example of where to find table name and first two variable names in Infoshare\&quot; src=\&quot;\/assets\/Uploads\/Tools\/CSV-files-for-download\/Infoshare-variable-names-2__ResizedImageWzYwMCw0MTJd.png\&quot; loading=\&quot;lazy\&quot; class=\&quot;leftAlone ss-htmleditorfield-file image\&quot;&gt;\n\